      "raw_response": "To determine the correct answer, we need to consider the trends in food affordability in the United States. Studies have shown that the real price of food has increased over recent decades, reflecting inflation and changes in food production and distribution costs.\n\nFor instance, a study published in the Journal of Food Distribution Research found that food prices have been increasing at a rate that is slightly higher than the overall inflation rate, indicating that the real price of food has indeed increased (Source: [1]).\n\nThis aligns with the findings of the Economic Research Service (ERS) of the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA), which reports that the cost of a basic food basket has risen, making it harder for many households to afford adequate food (Source: [2]).\n\nOption B (\"The real price of food increased\") is supported by these findings and is a correct statement.\n\nANSWER: B",
